WEBVTT

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.150
Thank you for coming.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.830
No, not at all.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.800
So what can I do for you today?

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:34.840
Actually, I'm planning on holding 
a western-style tea party.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.150
A western-style... tea party, huh?

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:43.270
It will be something more relaxed, though.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.090
Do you mean one of those "girls' parties"

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.860
that are popular at the moment?

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.450
Yes.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.610
Having a cheerful chat 
with snacks and drinks.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.020
So you'd like me to arrange 
a girls' party, then?

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.240
Yes.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.870
But a rather special one.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.020
Special? What do you mean?

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:04.460
For instance, the number of attendees.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:05.990
Number?

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:06.960
Will there be many?

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:09.230
The opposite.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.550
Myself and one other.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:16.760
I have invited Yagyuu Sekishuusai.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.960
Just one?

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.700
Are you sure?

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:21.590
Yes.

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:24.520
And there's one absolute condition.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.730
Condition?

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:26.980
What's that?

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:29.810
The snacks must be super-hot.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.340
S-Super-hot?

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:37.740
Do you mean you want them spicy?

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:38.660
Indeed.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:40.330
Super-hot.

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:44.490
Food that will destroy your 
mouth with a single bite.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.080
Thank you.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:48.400
Why do you want that?

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.270
I was once the student 
of Kamiizumi Nobutsuna-sama.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:54.050
Yes, I heard

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:55.920
that you've studied under many

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.310
masters of the blade, 
besides Bokuden-sama.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:02.190
Sekishuusai was with me there.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:06.020
I was the younger pupil, and she the older.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:07.650
I see.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:09.530
Then, even though you were the shogun,

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:12.490
she outranked you during training.

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:13.510
That's right.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.100
The opposite of what it usually is.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.810
For that reason, Sekishuusai 
would often play

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:19.990
pranks on me during training.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.400
Sekishuusai-sama did such a thing?

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.080
The worst was when
she would spice up my food.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:31.080
She would mix mustard or 
wasabi in it once in a while.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.340
That's terrible.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.140
Yes.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:38.920
So I'm going to have my
revenge at this girls' party.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:22.400
Welcome, Sekishuusai-dono.

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:26.180
How long has it been since 
we've had a chance to talk?

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:29.750
I didn't see you during the 
matter with Bokuden-dono.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:31.360
So it's been a long time.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:35.650
Yes. I think it's been since we 
studied under Kamiizumi-sama.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:39.620
You were a very great help to 
your younger student then.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:40.920
Yes. A very great help.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.920
Not at all.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:47.590
Just thinking about it makes 
my heart and my mouth ache.

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:52.570
Rather than bittersweet memories,
they were just bitter.

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:54.950
You're the shogun now, Yoshiteru-sama.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:58.190
You shouldn't dwell on such things.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.630
I went too far. I regret it.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:02.880
That's right.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.320
Of course, it's all in the past.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:08.160
Please, come this way.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.000
I've brought this as a present.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:19.540
A katana I received from Kamiizumi-sama.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:21.120
What's this?

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:24.970
Our master didn't have any 
particular blade she favored.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:25.930
Indeed.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:30.910
So she would give the blades 
she was offered to anyone.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.630
This was a gift to her from a

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.500
rich merchant and she gave it to me.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.060
It certainly is a splendid blade.

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:38.520
You're giving it to me?

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:40.020
Yes, of course.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:43.030
But it's hard to believe someone like you

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:47.220
would give me something 
like this for free...

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.070
That's right.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:53.040
I'm not a nice and friendly 
person like that.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.520
I'm sorry.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.190
That's not what I meant.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:59.060
Of course it is.

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:01.150
If you're going to accuse 
me of stinginess,

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:03.000
then I have my own ideas.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.810
I didn't call you stingy...

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:06.570
No, you did and that's fine.

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:08.500
But I have a condition 
for giving it to you.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:10.050
Please, calm yourself.

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:12.090
I'm not upset.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:14.120
I have a condition, is all.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.800
I can't give it to such a petty person.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.480
Especially someone who can't get

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.830
over the past and is plotting revenge.

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:22.560
Gulp.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:27.890
If, for example, my snacks 
were spicy today,

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:30.170
I couldn't give it to you.

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:32.780
Of course, I'm sure that's not the case.

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:37.720
No, of course.

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:39.580
It's not.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:52.930
Here you are.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:57.140
Although, I suppose I've gotten too excited.

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:59.310
I apologize.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:01.850
Our snacks are here.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:03.350
Let's enjoy ourselves.

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:05.020
Yes...

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:15.300
I'm sure the cream puff isn't spicy, right?

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:17.850
No, of course not.

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:19.500
Then take a big bite.

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:23.750
I've started one of those "diet" things.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.620
Diets are taboo at girls' parties.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:29.240
Snacks, cake slices, even stews.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:30.700
The goal of such a party is to eliminate stress

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:32.800
by eating without 
worrying about weight gain.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:35.260
Now take a big bite.

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:36.900
Go on.

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:50.950
What's wrong?

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.300
It shouldn't be spicy.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.660
If it is, you can't have the katana.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:59.120
Where are you going?

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:00.800
There's still more.

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:01.720
But...

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:03.930
Now finish your snack.

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:05.380
You wouldn't be so rude

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:07.480
as to leave your seat 
during a meal, right?

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:17.730
<i>Water! Water!</i>

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:21.660
What are you doing?

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:24.590
I'll let you go when 
you admit it's spicy.

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:26.690
I'm not gonna admit it!

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:30.840
If it's not spicy, then why 
not return to your seat?

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.900
I won't let you go otherwise.

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:34.590
Come on.

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:38.410
Spicy! It's spicy!

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:44.290
Revenge after all these 
years? How petty.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:48.210
And you're never gonna outsmart me.

00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:56.820
You shouldn't drink directly 
from the bottle, it's uncouth.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:58.810
Rikyuu, a glass for this.

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:00.760
You devilish monster!

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.620
Actually, this is red pepper juice.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.200
I pretended to drink it.

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:31.160
We're going down together!

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:32.910
Let me go!

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:35.300
No, I won't!

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:36.590
Here!

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:42.970
It's not spicy!

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:52.730
Well then, let me see that sword.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:55.900
The snacks were spicy, 
so you can't have it.

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:59.780
You didn't eat them, so 
what's the problem?

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:02.220
You tried to trick me, 
that's the problem!

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:04.580
I'm not giving it to someone so petty!

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.870
You're dragging out something 
that doesn't matter,

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.480
like an old woman.

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:11.770
I drank the juice, so I wasn't fine!

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:13.890
You were just talking about how good

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:15.840
you were at tricking people.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.130
I wouldn't lose in a fair fight.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:21.770
All right.

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:23.380
Let's play a game, then.

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:24.670
A game?

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:28.100
Russian roulette, which is often 
performed at these girls' parties.

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:32.750
There are several cake slices, 
only one of which is spicy.

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:36.210
The person who chooses it 
and eats it loses.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:38.650
I told you, you're not getting the katana.

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:43.450
Then why don't we each bet 
what we both love most?

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:44.950
What we love most?

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:50.020
We generals all have something 
we care about the most, right?

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:52.580
Like a secret treasure.

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:13.620
So what brings you here?

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:14.860
What else?

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:16.650
I'm here for your treasures.

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:21.160
Yoshiteru-sama and Sekishuusai-sama 
are both here right now.

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:24.130
Of course, I'll take both of theirs, too.

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:26.440
By force if necessary.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:30.520
So Nobunaga-sama is here.

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:32.510
Come to think of it,

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:35.490
I've heard that Nobunaga is 
taking all the secret treasures.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:38.130
So she heard us say
"secret treasure" and came?

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.460
Don't be stupid.

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:41.330
No, it's possible.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:43.980
I'm told there have been 
several victims already.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:46.020
So she's after both of our treasures?

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:48.100
I'm not sure what to do.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:52.480
My intention was to put both 
of our prides on the line.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:54.990
But I've heard that if you lose your treasure,

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:58.030
you can never 
go back to our world.

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:01.200
Which means we can't give it to 
her under any circumstances.

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:06.200
So we should start...

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:08.700
...by getting rid of Nobunaga.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.710
Can I take that as an alliance then?

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:13.980
Of course.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.710
But how do we do it?

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:19.510
We have her join us in Russian roulette.

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:20.910
I see.

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:22.790
So you think you can win?

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:24.840
Yes. I've had a mark made

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.510
on the spicy cake slice we'll be using.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:31.260
So you were planning on 
cheating from the start?

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:32.520
N-No.

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:37.340
That's pretty cheap.

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:40.590
Now's not the time for that!

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:43.200
Fine. We can discuss it later.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:44.820
So what's this mark?

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:45.570
Right.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:50.130
The cherry decoration 
is slightly off center.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:53.200
That is the spicy cake.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.250
I see.

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:57.180
It's very slight.

00:12:57.180 --> 00:13:01.260
Unless you had a very keen eye,
you'd never notice.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:04.580
So let us both avoid that.

00:13:04.580 --> 00:13:05.260
Understood?

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.230
Then send Nobunaga in.

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:12.020
We know why you're here.

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:14.310
That makes this easy, then.

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:18.730
But we cannot simply hand them over.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.540
I know that.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:23.830
That's why I usually take them by force.

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:26.940
We were just about to have a game.

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:28.690
A game? What game?

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:30.540
I'll explain.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:33.500
And if you win, you may 
have our treasures.

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:41.050
Out of these six cake
slices, two are super-hot.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:45.040
So you lose if you eat 
a spicy one, huh?

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:46.640
That's right.

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:48.930
We've prepared a habanero cake.

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:49.800
Habanero?

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:53.690
A particularly spicy pepper.

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:56.140
It's several times hotter than the spicy

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:57.770
cream puff I just served.

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:00.400
What were you guys doing?

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:06.400
We will each eat one cake 
in turn until they're gone.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:09.090
But it sounds fun.

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:11.160
If you eat it, it's spicy enough

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.360
that drinking something won't help.

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:16.370
You'll lose your ability to fight back.

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:17.920
It's that spicy?

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:21.510
The treasures can easily be taken, then.

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:22.790
I see.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:25.170
It's nice and convenient for me, then.

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.180
Let's get started.

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:30.570
Okay, I will start.

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:31.510
One second.

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:33.090
What?

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:37.280
It looks like two of these cake 
slices are different from the rest.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:38.940
Why?

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.360
Intuition. That's all.

00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:42.720
But they really are different.

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:44.260
That's not true.

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:48.150
I'm not making it up. 
It's really obvious.

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:51.620
So you want to quit?

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.450
You should leave, then.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:56.040
Oh, shut up.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:59.780
I'm not quitting the game. I'm just saying something's not right.

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:01.710
Since you prepared these cake slices,

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:05.030
you should want to clear your name.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:09.220
Very well. Let's have Rikyuu remake them.

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:11.360
That's fine.

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:16.250
Rikyuu, remake these two cake 
slices and shuffle them.

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:24.110
You guys are still suspicious.

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:26.450
Are you saying there's something else?

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:28.440
No, there's no problem, but...

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:29.990
Something's suspicious.

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:31.330
What?

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:32.800
I'm not letting you 
make anything else up.

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:34.330
That's right. It's not proper.

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:35.850
Shut up.

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:37.150
Oh, I know.

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:39.760
Let's all eat with our eyes closed.

00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:43.580
You're not going to refuse are you?

00:15:47.970 --> 00:15:51.880
<i>Now it's all even.</i>

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:55.390
<i>So only one of us is going to survive.</i>

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:59.190
So the last one standing 
gets all the treasures.

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:00.760
If we lose our treasures...

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:03.160
...we can't go back to our world.

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:06.400
That just means your luck 
wasn't good enough.

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:08.610
One wins and goes home.

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:11.110
Two lose and stay here.

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:14.160
I'm going to win, no matter what.

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:16.530
The first one to pick...

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:17.410
Will be me.

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:29.370
Yoshiteru-sama, I want to say 
something before the game.

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:30.380
What?

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:36.560
I loved you more than any 
of the other students.

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:38.750
Everything I've done 
was because of that.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:41.390
Why are you telling me this now?

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:45.300
If I lose my treasure, I can't go back.

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:47.470
Which means there's a possibility

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:50.610
this game will be the 
last time I see you.

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:53.650
Sekishuusai...

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:11.230
Sekishuusai!

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:13.810
No...

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:16.470
Looks like one of us is out.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:19.220
If I'd known, I would've done it myself.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:20.680
It's your turn now.

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:22.980
No, regrets won't help.

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:25.890
Now I just have to trust fate.

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:27.480
Just hurry up and eat.

00:17:28.370 --> 00:17:29.770
I know!

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:31.690
I just need a moment.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:46.800
Jeez, hurry up.

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:48.180
Even if it's for the treasure,

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:51.400
I already know I'm 
going to win this game.

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:01.680
This cake is pretty good.

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:04.680
Three left.

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:08.700
And one of them is super-hot.

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:10.190
It's my turn now, right?

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.300
<i>But...</i>

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:17.700
Sekishuusai.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:22.210
I enjoyed those days I 
trained with you, too.

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:26.540
Actually, I loved when we
played tricks on each other.

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:29.240
You'd make me eat something spicy

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:31.140
and I would drop you in a hole.

00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:33.060
I'd trick you into thinking 
there was a bear,

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:34.900
and you'd freeze my bathwater.

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:37.680
So you were getting back 
at her, Yoshiteru-sama!

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:39.180
Yoshiteru-sama...

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:42.730
I played pranks on you
because I loved you.

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:45.750
So I was sad when you left.

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:48.590
That was all I wanted to say.

00:18:48.590 --> 00:18:54.940
Yoshiteru-sama, I played those 
tricks because I looked up to you.

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:57.060
And this time,

00:18:57.060 --> 00:19:01.250
I wanted to be honest with 
myself and make up...

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:03.490
That's why I brought that katana.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:04.680
Sekishuusai...

00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:13.550
It wasn't that one?!

00:19:13.550 --> 00:19:16.030
Then it's one of these two!

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:30.270
Water! Water! Water!

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:32.050
I won.

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:37.120
<i>Now Sekishuusai and Nobunaga's 
treasures belong to me.</i>

00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:42.570
<i>But even if I return to my world alone,</i>

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:44.800
<i>what good does that do me?</i>

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:49.490
<i>I'd never see her again...</i>

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:53.910
Rikyuu.

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:55.560
Bring me super-hot tea.

00:19:56.720 --> 00:19:59.530
Yoshiteru-sama, what are you saying?

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:01.830
Just make me some.

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:03.680
You may ignore Nobunaga.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:06.930
Yoshiteru-sama, does that mean...

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:08.400
Yes. That's right.

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:10.680
I'm prepared.

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:19.690
Here.

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:22.200
Yoshiteru-sama.

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:25.800
Sekishuusai...

00:20:42.940 --> 00:20:44.890
Yoshiteru-sama...

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:51.970
Yoshiteru-sama...

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:56.020
Sekishuusai...

00:21:02.550 --> 00:21:04.760
So spicy.

00:21:05.650 --> 00:21:07.460
What is this?

00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:11.700
They've both decided to 
remain in this world.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.830
This is a beautiful friendship.

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:19.210
Or rather, a sisterhood whose tale should be

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:21.080
told throughout the ages.

00:21:21.810 --> 00:21:24.090
Well, I don't understand.

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:26.430
But you guys are idiots.

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:29.430
But if that's what you want...

00:21:58.030 --> 00:21:58.920
So spicy.

00:23:46.600 --> 00:23:50.320
Next time it's the 
Sunshine Ruler, Liu Bei.

00:23:51.290 --> 00:23:55.450
Next time on Sengoku 
Collection: "Sunshine Ruler."

00:23:56.160 --> 00:23:58.610
Hold on, she's from the wrong country!
